{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100, "noise": "N2"}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 135, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a missing input-output residual shortcut helps far more than replacing an existing learned op on that edge."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "In skip-dominated, parameter-free cells an extra identity path to the output degrades accuracy instead of helping."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Pooling-dominated cells lack convolutions, so an added identity shortcut further dilutes learned features and hurts."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing edge 0->3 when edge 2->3 is absent can disconnect or severely starve the output node."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Placing a conv on an empty input-output edge adds a new path rather than merely swapping ops."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Without the 0->3 shortcut, a skip on edge 2->3 supplies a needed residual path, whereas with it present the swap mainly removes conv capacity."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "In skip-heavy cells edge 5 is often the only convolution, so replacing it with skip collapses learning capacity."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "When edge 2->3 is absent, a conv on edge 1->3 becomes the main conv route into the output and adds much more value."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 2->3 absent, turning the 1->3 conv into pooling removes the main conv path to the output."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Without edge 2->3, cutting edge 0->1 kills node 1 and leaves the output with only the input shortcut."}], "tok": 17401, "bad": 0, "probes": [[["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "none", "none", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "none", "none", "none", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "none", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "none", 